        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "The article argues that forward-thinking CIOs should embed compliance as a design principle rather than an afterthought, adopting a controls-by-design approach that treats regulatory frameworks like the EU AI Act and DORA as architectural inputs. Using payments as a case study, it shows that proactive governance enables faster fraud detection, reduced false positives, and customer trustΓÇöciting a CSG Forte and IBM partnership that cut fraud losses by 50-70%. The piece emphasizes cross-functional alignment and strategic partnerships as essential to turning regulatory readiness into a competitive differentiator.",
