        "date":  "2026-06-23",
        "theme":  "Philosophy",
        "summary":  "Thornton May argues that enterprise technology leaders are making a strategic mistake by over-engineering systems for simplicity and under-investing in human AI literacy, noting that only 40% of companies provide generative AI training to users. He draws on Deloitte research and frames \u0027knowledge pumping\u0027ΓÇösustained executive education, anchor visuals, and data storytellingΓÇöas the primary lever for realizing AI\u0027s value, rather than further system simplification. The piece cites Sam Altman\u0027s view that AI missionaries will beat mercenaries, cautioning against purely profit-driven AI narratives.",
